    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d497">

                <pb facs="0666" n="546" xml:id="pg546"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Minister Powell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-05-11"><hi rendition="#italic">May 11,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 697.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose copy of a letter from Mr. Elie A.
                        Mansour,<anchor n="a" xml:id="d497-f1"/> who alleges that he is an American
                    citizen and that he is suffering damages from the Haitian Government because of
                    their refusal to issue a license to carry on his business.</p>
                <p>You will examine the case and report to the Department.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. B. Loomis.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
